course: dictionary
lesson: 8176
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «Most stories climb a story mountain: an opening, a build-up, a problem, a resolution where the problem is sorted, and an ending.» The words around resolution are problem and sorted, so here it means the part where the problem is solved.
explain: Look at where the word sits in the sentence. «Stories often use a story mountain: the opening at the bottom, the build-up climbing, the problem at the top, then the resolution and the ending on the way down» shows the resolution comes after the problem, on the way down. Always ask: what happens just before and just after this word?
explain: The same word can mean something different in another place. A New Year's resolution is a firm decision to do or not do something. On a computer, resolution means how sharp and detailed a screen or picture is, measured in pixels. If a problem is being solved, it is the story or fairness meaning; if someone is deciding to change, it is the decision meaning.
fact: Resolution means the part of a story where the problem is solved, coming after the problem and before the ending.
fact: A story mountain has five parts: opening, build-up, problem, resolution and ending.
fact: A resolution can also be a firm decision, such as a «New Year's resolution».
fact: In PSHE, «conflict resolution» means solving a fight or argument fairly.
fact: In computing, «high resolution» means a sharp, detailed picture, measured in pixels.
exercise: In a story mountain, which part comes straight after the problem? | The build-up, climbing | The opening, at the bottom | The title | *The resolution, where the problem is sorted
exercise: Maya says, «I made a resolution to read every day.» What does resolution mean here? | The last page of a book | *A firm decision to do something | A sharp picture on a screen | A solved argument between two friends
exercise: Which phrase means a sharp, detailed picture, measured in pixels? | conflict resolution | New Year's resolution | story mountain | *high resolution
test: The class had a fight, but the teacher helped them find a fair way to end it. What does conflict resolution mean? | Making a New Year's wish | *Solving a fight or argument fairly | Writing a story about a fight | Starting a new fight
test: Which part of a story comes after the problem and before the ending? | The build-up | *The resolution | The opening | The title
exam: In the sentence «The problem was at the top of the mountain, then the resolution came on the way down», what does resolution mean? | *The part where the problem is sorted | A sharp picture on a screen | A firm decision to change | An official vote by a council
